d-500/30\">\r\n556:                  Sec 44AD Presumptive\r\n557-                </span>\r\n558-              </h4>\r\n559-              <p class=\"text-[10px] text-slate-400\">Deterministic Tax Calculation & Gemini 2.5 Flash Advisory</p>\r\n560-            </div>\r\n561-          </div>\r\n--\r\n578-          <div class=\"bg-slate-800/80 rounded-xl p-3 border border-slate-700/80 flex flex-col justify-between\">\r\n579-            <span class=\"text-[9px] font-bold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider block\">Pill 1 • Recommended Form</span>\r\n580-            <div class=\"mt-1 font-bold text-xs text-emerald-300\">\r\n581-              ${calculated_tax.recommended_form}\r\n582-            </div>\r\n583:            <span class=\"text-[9px] text-slate-400 mt-1 block\">Presumptive Scheme under Sec 44AD</span>\r\n584-          </div>\r\n585-\r\n586-          <!-- Pill 2: Deemed Net Profit -->\r\n587-          <div class=\"bg-slate-800/80 rounded-xl p-3 border border-slate-700/80 flex flex-col justify-between\">\r\n588-            <span class=\"text-[9px] font-bold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider block\">Pill 2 • Deemed Net Profit</span>\r\n--\r\n604-        </div>\r\n605-\r\n606-        <!-- REAL-TIME SHOP TURNOVER & CASH RATIO SLIDER -->\r\n607-        <div class=\"bg-slate-800/40 rounded-xl p-3 border border-slate-700/50 space-y-2 text-xs\">\r\n608-          <div class=\"flex items-center justify-between text-[11px] text-slate-300\">\r\n609:            <span class=\"font-bold\">Adjust Digital Receipts Ratio (Sec 44AD Profit: 6% Digital vs 8% Cash):</span>\r\n610-            <span class=\"font-mono font-bold text-emerald-300\" id=\"label-digital-ratio\">${calculated_tax.digital_percent}% Digital (${calculated_tax.cash_percent}% Cash)</span>\r\n611-          </div>\r\n612-          <input \r\n613-            type=\"range\" \r\n614-            min=\"0\" \r\n"}
{"step_index":1850,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:19:43Z","input_tokens":2820,"cache_read_tokens":64447,"output_tokens":3971,"thinking":"The existing widget within the \"AuditScorecard.js\" file is related to a specific presumptive taxation section. The user's request is for a dedicated tab encompassing a customizable tax engine. This suggests that the existing widget is insufficient and a new, more comprehensive tax and ITR filing tab is required, separate from the invoice math audit.\n\n\nThe existing invoice math audit tab remains unchanged. A new tab for tax and ITR filing is needed. This tab will house a customizable tax engine allowing users to select tax regimes and filing types like regular business (ITR-3) or presumptive taxation (ITR-4). Presumptive taxation will have interactive sliders for digital versus cash transactions.\n\n\nA customizable tax engine requires interactive controls for presumptive taxation calculations, including sliders for digital and cash sales percentages, affecting the net taxable profit. Deductions and exemptions need panels tailored to the selected tax regime, with specific inputs for old regimes and automatic application of standard deductions or rebates for new regimes. A dynamic engine will compute tax slabs, surcharge, cess, and total estimated tax payable with effective tax rates.\n\nThe module also integrates a GST Input Tax Credit (ITC) audit card, reading verified invoice data and allowing users to specify business use to determine ITC eligibility. Finally, an export function enables the download of the complete tax computation and ITC details in CSV or PDF format.\n\n\nThe tab navigation bar is correctly placed within `ReviewWorkspace.js`, directly below the top navigation bar. Tab 1 will present the existing invoice audit view without modification. Tab 2 will present the new tax engine view, which will share reactive state with the `invoice`, `audit`, and `taxSettings` within `app.js`.\n\n\nThe active tab state should be managed within the application instance (`app.js`) to ensure it persists across re-renders and input changes. The `app.recomputeEverything()` function and the `render()` method are critical for maint\n<truncated 240 bytes>\nlculation modes: a general mode with expense inputs and a presumptive taxation mode with digital/cash sales sliders and editable profit percentages. These calculations determine net taxable profit differently for each mode.\n\nCustomizable deduction panels will be implemented based on the selected tax regime. Old regimes will require manual input for deductions like 80C and 80D. New regimes will automatically apply a standard deduction and indicate eligibility for full rebates under Section 87A.\n\n\nA prominent badge will display \"₹0 Tax Payable (100% Tax Rebate under Sec 87A)\" if taxable income is within the ₹7,00,000 threshold. The tax slab computation will reflect the new tax regime, starting with 0% up to ₹3,00,000 and 5% between ₹3,00,001 and ₹7,00,000.  The system must also account for the Old Tax Regime slabs, showing nil up to ₹2,50,000, 5% between ₹2,50,001 and ₹5,00,000, and 20% between ₹5,00,001 and ₹10,00,000. A 4% Health & Education Cess will be applied. A live breakdown table, gross tax calculation, and Sec 87A rebate display will be included in the presentation.\n\n\nThe tax computation presentation will include the 87A rebate (if applicable), 4% Health & Education Cess, total estimated income tax payable, and the effective tax rate. The effective tax rate calculation will be either (Total Tax / Gross Revenue) * 100 or (Total Tax / Taxable Profit) * 100.\n\nThe GST ITC audit card will read verified invoice data to show eligible ITC (CGST, SGST, IGST, and their sum). It will include a toggle for business use, flagging ineligible ITC under Section 17(5) or marking 100% eligible ITC. It will also validate the supplier's GSTIN. A net cash GST outflow estimator will be included, calculating net payable GST by subtracting eligible ITC from gross output GST. This is designed to show potential cash savings through ITC.\n\nA single-click export function will generate a CSV file or trigger a PDF view, containing the full tax computation, breakdown, regime comparison, deductions, and slab details.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"grep -rn \\\"calculateTaxMetrics\\\" /Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Search calculateTaxMetrics usage\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
