{"step_index":1858,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:20:52Z","input_tokens":3801,"cache_read_tokens":76060,"output_tokens":16806,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nConsidering how the audit scorecard is calculated. There are two modes, Regular and Presumptive, each with its own formula for net profit. Mode A uses total expenses from cost of goods sold and operating expenses, while Mode B calculates profit based on digital and cash sales percentages. The `settings` object customizes these calculations through various parameters.\n\n\nCalculating taxable income based on the tax regime. The \"NEW\" regime employs a standard deduction and progressive tax slabs with potential Sec 87A rebate. The \"OLD\" regime uses specified deductions and different tax slabs.\n\n\nTax calculation involves slab-based progressive rates (5%, 20%, 30%) with a potential Sec 87A rebate for income below ₹5,00,000. A 4% Health & Education Cess applies to the net tax post-rebate. GST Input Tax Credit (ITC) eligibility depends on factors like resale status and GSTIN validity, potentially leading to blocked ITC under specific conditions.\n\n\nThe `netPayableCashGst` calculation now correctly handles eligible ITC, ensuring the output GST is non-negative. This is implemented in a backwards-compatible way to integrate seamlessly with existing `calculateTaxMetrics` function calls, providing comprehensive tax data. The UI for the tax filing dashboard is being designed to allow for customizable parameters, including tax regime selection and business filing scheme selection.\n\n\nConsidering the two modes for calculating net taxable profit. Mode A directly subtracts total expenses from gross revenue, while Mode B uses digital and cash sales percentages with custom profit inputs to estimate profit. The system provides an interactive slider and custom inputs to adjust these percentages.\n\nThe Old tax regime allows for custom deduction inputs for sections 80C and 80D, as well as a standard deduction, whereas the New regime automatically applies a standard deduction and indicates Sec 87A rebate eligibility. Dynamic tax slabs will be computed with a breakdown including surcharge/cess and\n<truncated 8403 bytes>\ntom profit percentages for digital/cash sales, displaying a live formula. Regular mode will have inputs for annual revenue, cost of goods sold, and operating expenses, also with a live formula. The UI will dynamically show the appropriate deductions based on the selected tax regime.\n\n\nAnalyzing UI component requirements for tax calculation display. Taxable income determination depends on the tax regime, either Old or New, and is interactive, with different deduction inputs. The New regime applies a ₹75,000 standard deduction, and the Old regime has customizable deduction inputs with caps. UI will display Section 87A rebate eligibility based on taxable income. A dynamic tax slab breakdown, including tax bracket, rate, taxable amount, and computed tax, will be presented in a visual table.\n\nThe system will display a mathematical summary of tax liability, including gross tax, rebate, net tax, cess, total estimated tax payable, and effective tax rate. An input tax credit (ITC) audit card will verify invoice data and determine ITC eligibility based on resale/capital use. A custom toggle will allow users to indicate purchase purpose, potentially flagging ineligible credits under Section 17(5).\n\n\nExamining Input Tax Credit (ITC) eligibility criteria. Purchases related to personal consumption, gifts, motor vehicles, or food/beverages are ineligible for GST ITC. Valid supplier GSTINs are verified, and an unregistered supplier triggers a warning. A \"Net Cash GST Outflow Estimator\" displays net payable GST after subtracting eligible ITC from gross output GST, with a savings badge showing direct cash savings via ITC.\n\nA \"1-Click Export\" button triggers a CSV download or print/PDF of the tax computation sheet. Changes to sliders, inputs, or toggles call `onUpdateTaxSettings`, triggering `recomputeEverything` in `app.js` and synchronously updating all metrics. Edge cases are being considered; revenue, COGS, and digital/cash ratios are clamped to valid ranges. Invalid input characters (commas, currency symbols) are handled.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"// Deterministic Tax & ITR Calculator for Small Indian Retail Shopkeepers\\n// Core Rule: \\\"Code does the math, deterministic calculations only\\\"\\nimport { round2 } from \\\"./auditEngine.js\\\";\\n\\n/**\\n * Calculates comprehensive tax computation across New & Old Regimes,\\n * Section 44AD Presumptive (ITR-4) vs Regular Business P&L (ITR-3),\\n * Dynamic Slab-by-Slab breakdown with 4% Cess, and GST ITC Cash Outflow.\\n *\\n * @param {Object} invoice\\n * @param {Object} audit\\n * @param {Object} [settings]\\n * @returns {Object} Full comprehensive tax computation\\n */\\nexport function calculateComprehensiveTax(invoice = {}, audit = {}, settings = {}) {\\n  // 1. Settings & Defaults\\n  const regime = settings.regime === \\\"OLD\\\" ? \\\"OLD\\\" : \\\"NEW\\\"; // \\\"NEW\\\" is default\\n  const filingScheme = settings.filingScheme === \\\"REGULAR\\\" ? \\\"REGULAR\\\" : \\\"PRESUMPTIVE\\\"; // \\\"PRESUMPTIVE\\\" is default\\n  const annualRevenue = Math.max(0, Number(settings.annualRevenue !== undefined && settings.annualRevenue !== null ? settings.annualRevenue : 3600000));\\n  \\n  // Current bill verified GST\\n  const cgst = round2(Number(invoice.cgst) || 0);\\n  const sgst = round2(Number(invoice.sgst) || 0);\\n  const igst = round2(Number(invoice.igst) || 0);\\n  const totalBillGst = round2(cgst + sgst + igst);\\n  const billSubtotal = round2(Number(invoice.subtotal) || Number(invoice.calculated_subtotal) || (audit && audit.sum_items) || 0);\\n\\n  // Business Resale Toggle (Sec 17(5))\\n  const isBusinessResale = settings.isBusinessResale !== false;\\n  const isGstinValid = audit ? (audit.gstinValid !== false) : true;\\n\\n  let itcStatus = \\\"ELIGIBLE\\\";\\n  let itcStatusLabel = \\\"100% Eligible ITC for GSTR-3B Set-off\\\";\\n  let eligibleItc = 0;\\n  let blockedItc = 0;\\n\\n  if (!isBusinessResale) {\\n    itcStatus = \\\"BLOCKED_17_5\\\";\\n    itcStatusLabel = \\\"Ineligible / Blocked Credit under Sec 17(5)\\\";\\n    blockedItc = totalBillGst;\\n    eligibleItc = 0;\\n  } else if (!isGstinValid) {\\n    itcStatus = \\\"MISSING_GSTIN\\\";\\n    itcStatusLabel = \\\"Restricted: Missing\n<truncated 11263 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/taxCalculator.js\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking","tool_calls"]}
