{"step_index":1860,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:22:41Z","input_tokens":16806,"cache_read_tokens":79937,"output_tokens":14876,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nConsidering two modes for calculating Net Taxable Profit: a detailed method using revenue and expenses, and a presumptive method based on digital versus cash sales with adjustable profit percentages. The system should allow for custom deductions and exemptions based on the selected tax regime, including standard deductions and Section 87A rebate. A dynamic tax slab engine will compute the final estimated income tax payable, along with the effective tax rate. Also, there will be an input tax credit audit feature for GST purposes.\n\n\nThe system will classify purchases for ITC eligibility, distinguishing between ineligible purchases and those eligible for 100% ITC set-off. A net cash GST outflow estimator will calculate the payable GST after deducting eligible ITC from gross output GST. The output will be formatted using a currency formatter.\n\nCSV export functionality will be implemented, generating a UTF-8 BOM encoded CSV file that will include report headers, date, assessment year, invoice context, tax planning parameters, and profit computation details, formatted as either regular or presumptive.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"// Component: Tax & ITR Filing Dashboard (Tab 2)\\n// Fully customizable tax planning engine for Indian small retail shopkeepers\\nimport { calculateComprehensiveTax } from \\\"../utils/taxCalc